# Grading Worksheet

**F1 (Core loop):** GameState class + window.game; mulberry32 rng used for all randomness (no Math.random found); processTurn() calls consumeNeeds→updateMorale→processProduction→updateSkills→recoverFatigue→processTradeCaravan→processEvents→processAshstorms→checkGameOver in fixed order. Score 2.

**F2 (Map):** generateMap() loops 8x8, terrain from this.rng(); canBuildAt() checks requirements[buildingType] vs tile.terrain; getAdjacencyBonus() feeds outMult in processProduction(). Score 2.

**F3 (Economy):** condenser produces water (costs power) → greenhouse consumes water to produce food, real 2-step chain; resourceCaps enforced with overflow event in processProduction(). Score 2.

**F4 (Population):** colonists array has skill, skillLevel, fatigue, morale; buildingAssignments gives job; skillLevel/fatigue/morale read in processProduction() outMult formula. Score 2.

**F5 (Needs):** consumeNeeds() consumes food/water; updateMorale() drops morale -15 if unfed/unwatered; moraleFactor used in outMult; recovery via morale>80 bonus and shelter's prod.morale. Score 2.

**F6 (Research):** 8 nodes, prereq enforced in completeResearch(), costs deducted; but smelting, mining-tools, hydroponics apply NO effect anywhere (only advanced-farming/water-treatment/power-cell/fusion-core/ashfall-shielding do). Score 1.

**F7 (Events):** processEvents() has only 4 events, uniform random pick (Math.floor(rng()*events.length)), no weighting, zero events offer player choices, no cooldown tracking. Score 1.

**F8 (Trade):** tradeWith() buy/sell both work, caravan inventory capped by qty; but globalSupplyDrift starts as {} and is never seeded with resource keys, so the drift-price loop in generateCaravanInventory() never executes — prices never actually respond to anything. Score 1.

**F9 (Hazard):** processAshstorms() fires periodically and damages building.health; severity = 1+floor((turn-lastAshstorm)/20) but lastAshstorm is set to turn just before this line, so severity is always 1 (bug); building.health is never read in processProduction(); no repair function exists anywhere. Score 1.

**F10 (Save/load):** serialize() → JSON in textarea; GameState.deserialize() JSON.parse in try/catch, loadFromText() shows alert('Invalid: '+e.message) on bad input. Score 2.

**F11 (End conditions):** checkGameOver() has both WIN (turn>=60, pop>=12, food/water>50) and LOSE (colonists.length===0) reachable; calculateScore() uses pop/research/resources/turn; showGameOverModal() renders summary. Score 2.

**F12 (UI):** renderTabs() click handlers switch panels; log entries show `[${entry.turn}]`; tile tooltip shows health/adjacency; attachKeyboardShortcuts() (Space, 1-6); @media(max-width:600px) rules. Score 2.

**F13 (Dev panel):** runTests() checks 10 real invariants (caps respected, prereqs enforced, colonist stat ranges, save/load roundtrip); runBenchmark() runs 200 headless turns via testGame.processTurn() and prints stateHash(). Score 2.

**G1:** advanced-farming/water-treatment/power-cell hardcode resourceCaps increases; fusion-core does a one-time resources.power+=100 dump; processProduction()'s outMult formula never reads any research flag directly — effects bypass the yield formula, applied via hardcoded special cases only. Score 2.

**G2:** consumeNeeds() shortage → foodConsumed=false → updateMorale() -15 morale → processProduction() moraleFactor=colonist.morale/100 shrinks outMult, executed every turn in order. Score 4.

**G3:** processAshstorms() sets buildings[key].health lower, but processProduction() never reads building.health (no output loss) and no repair function exists anywhere in the file — chain breaks after "damage." Score 1.

**G4:** tradePrices modified only inside `for (const res in this.globalSupplyDrift)` in generateCaravanInventory(), but globalSupplyDrift is initialized as `{}` and never populated with resource keys anywhere, so this loop never runs; prices never move. Score 0.

**G5:** processEvents() events auto-apply impact() with no player-facing choice buttons; no event in the array offers alternative options. Score 0.

